---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import FinancialStatementKey from "../../components/FinancialStatementKey.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/indas/indas40.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope & Applicability" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Identifying Investment Property" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Initial Measurement — Cost" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Subsequent Measurement — The Mandatory Cost Model" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Mandatory Fair Value Disclosure" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Why Ind AS 40 Prohibits the Fair Value Model — Indian Rationale" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Transfers To/From Investment Property" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Disclosure" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Ind AS 40 vs IAS 40 — Full Comparison" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">

    <!-- ============ SECTION 1 — CONCEPTUAL FRAMEWORK LINK ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Same rental/appreciation definition as IAS 40, narrower Indian measurement choice</div>
        <div class="principle">Ind AS 40 shares IAS 40's core DEFINITION — investment property is land/buildings held to earn RENTAL income or for CAPITAL APPRECIATION, rather than for use in production/supply or sale in the ordinary course of business. Where Ind AS 40 genuinely diverges is SUBSEQUENT MEASUREMENT: IAS 40 offers a CHOICE between the cost model and the fair value model (with fair value changes through P&amp;L); Ind AS 40 REMOVES this choice, mandating the COST MODEL only.</div>
        <div class="elabel">HOW IND AS 40 MAPS TO THE FRAMEWORK</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span><strong>Reliability over relevance trade-off</strong> — Indian standard-setters favoured the RELIABILITY of a cost-based measurement (avoiding potentially volatile or difficult-to-verify property valuations flowing through P&amp;L) over the added relevance a fair value model might offer</span>
          <span><strong>Consistency with Ind AS 16</strong> — mandating the cost model for investment property aligns its measurement approach more closely with Ind AS 16's OWN predominant Indian practice (see Ind AS 16 poster) for owner-occupied property</span>
        </div>
        <div class="note">This is one of the MOST significant, well-documented Ind AS divergences from its IFRS counterpart — comparable in weight to Ind AS 20's grant presentation divergence and Ind AS 1's format divergence.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cs">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Cost model vs fair value model — the core divergence</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-1-1-1"><span>Model</span><span>IAS 40</span><span>Ind AS 40</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-1-1-1"><span>Cost model</span><span>Available (choice)</span><span>MANDATORY</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-1-1-1"><span>Fair value model (P&amp;L)</span><span>Available (choice)</span><span>PROHIBITED for measurement</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 2 — SCOPE & DEFINITIONS ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope &amp; Applicability</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw">
        <div class="ctitle cw">What Ind AS 40 covers</div>
        <div class="principle">Ind AS 40 applies to recognition, measurement, and disclosure of investment property — IDENTICAL scope to IAS 40 in terms of WHAT qualifies, but with the MANDATORY cost model overlay on subsequent measurement.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cd">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Key definitions you must know</div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Investment property</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">IDENTICAL definition to IAS 40 — property held to earn rentals or for capital appreciation, or both.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Owner-occupied property</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">Property held for use in production/supply, or administrative purposes — SCOPED OUT of Ind AS 40, governed by Ind AS 16 instead, identical distinction to IAS 40.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 3 — IDENTIFYING ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Identifying Investment Property</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Identical to IAS 40</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">The KEY distinguishing factor is whether cash flows are LARGELY INDEPENDENT of other entity assets (investment property) versus generated jointly with other assets used in operations — IDENTICAL classification test to IAS 40.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 4 — INITIAL MEASUREMENT ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Initial Measurement — Cost</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Identical to IAS 40</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Purchase price plus directly attributable expenditure (legal fees, property transfer taxes, other transaction costs) — IDENTICAL initial measurement to IAS 40.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 5 — MANDATORY COST MODEL (worked example) ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Subsequent Measurement — The Mandatory Cost Model</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">The core divergence, illustrated</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example 1: Cost model vs fair value model comparison</div>
          <div class="wk-body">An Indian real estate company holds a commercial building as investment property, purchased for ₹50,00,00,000 (with a 30-year useful life, no residual value), currently having a fair value of ₹75,00,00,000 after 5 years.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">
            Under IAS 40's FAIR VALUE model (NOT available under Ind AS 40): the property would be carried at ₹75,00,00,000, with a ₹25,00,00,000 cumulative fair value GAIN recognised through P&amp;L over the holding period.<br>
            Under Ind AS 40's MANDATORY COST MODEL: the property is carried at ₹50,00,00,000 less 5 years' accumulated depreciation (₹50,00,00,000 ÷ 30 × 5 = ₹8,33,33,333), i.e. approximately ₹41,66,66,667 — with NO fair value gain recognised in P&amp;L, though the ₹75,00,00,000 fair value MUST still be DISCLOSED in the notes.<br>
            This illustrates a MATERIAL difference in both balance sheet carrying amount and P&amp;L impact between the two frameworks.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 6 — MANDATORY FAIR VALUE DISCLOSURE ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Mandatory Fair Value Disclosure</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">A partial preservation of IAS 40's fair value relevance</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Even though the fair value MODEL is prohibited for measurement, Ind AS 40 STILL requires disclosure of investment property's FAIR VALUE in the notes — preserving SOME of the relevance IAS 40's fair value option would otherwise provide, without the P&amp;L volatility of full fair value measurement.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 7 — INDIAN RATIONALE ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Why Ind AS 40 Prohibits the Fair Value Model — Indian Rationale</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">The standard-setting rationale behind this divergence</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">India's standard-setters (the ICAI/ASB, feeding into the MCA's Ind AS notification process) determined that RELIABLE, VERIFIABLE fair valuations for real estate are NOT consistently available across India's diverse property markets (particularly outside major metros), and that introducing FAIR VALUE VOLATILITY into P&amp;L for investment property could distort reported profits in ways not reflective of genuine operating performance — a POLICY judgement resulting in the mandatory cost model, distinct from IAS 40's own global flexibility.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 8 — TRANSFERS ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Transfers To/From Investment Property</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Identical to IAS 40 (as applied under the cost model)</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Transfers to/from investment property occur when there is a CHANGE IN USE — since Ind AS 40 uses ONLY the cost model, transfers are recorded at the asset's EXISTING carrying amount (no fair value remeasurement gain/loss arises on transfer, unlike under IAS 40's fair value model option).</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 9 — DISCLOSURE ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Identical core disclosures to IAS 40, plus mandatory fair value note</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Depreciation method and useful lives used</span>
          <span>Gross carrying amount and accumulated depreciation reconciliation</span>
          <span>FAIR VALUE of investment property, even though cost model is used for measurement</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 10 — JUDGMENTS & ESTIMATES ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where management judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Classifying a property as investment property vs owner-occupied vs inventory (Ind AS 2)</span>
              <span>Change-in-use determination triggering transfers</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Fair value for MANDATORY disclosure purposes (even though not used for measurement)</span>
              <span>Useful life and residual value for depreciation</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="callout warn callout--chip callout--warn-flush">Users comparing an Indian Ind AS 40 preparer against a GLOBAL IFRS peer using the fair value model should be AWARE that reported carrying amounts and P&amp;L volatility from investment property can differ MATERIALLY, even where the underlying properties are economically comparable.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 11 — IND AS 40 vs IAS 40 ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Ind AS 40 vs IAS 40 — Full Comparison</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Comprehensive comparison table</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-12-1-1"><span>Feature</span><span>IAS 40</span><span>Ind AS 40</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-1-1"><span>Definition, initial measurement, transfers</span><span>Standard model</span><span>IDENTICAL — no substantive divergence</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-1-1"><span>Subsequent measurement</span><span>CHOICE: cost model OR fair value model (P&amp;L)</span><span>COST MODEL ONLY — fair value model PROHIBITED for measurement</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-1-1"><span>Fair value disclosure</span><span>Required if cost model chosen</span><span>ALWAYS required, regardless (mandatory disclosure-only fair value)</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">Ind AS 40's subsequent measurement is a MAJOR, well-documented divergence from IAS 40 — one of the most significant in the entire Ind AS suite, comparable in weight to Ind AS 20's grant presentation divergence and Ind AS 1's format divergence.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 12 — STATEMENT MAPPING ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Comprehensive event-to-statement mapping table</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event / transaction</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Investment property acquisition</span><span><span class="badge bs">Balance Sheet</span></span><span>At cost, identical to IAS 40's initial measurement</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-16-1-14"><span>Depreciation expense</span><span><span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> <span class="badge bs">Balance Sheet</span></span><span>MANDATORY under Ind AS 40's cost model — NOT applicable under IAS 40's fair value model</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Fair value change</span><span><span class="badge bp">Notes only</span></span><span>Disclosed, NEVER recognised in P&amp;L under Ind AS 40</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 13 — RELATED STANDARDS ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>IAS 40</span><span>The global counterpart standard, diverging significantly on subsequent measurement</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>Ind AS 16</span><span>Governs owner-occupied property, and supplies the cost/depreciation mechanics Ind AS 40 mirrors</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>Ind AS 113</span><span>Supplies the fair value measurement principles used for the mandatory disclosure-only fair value figure</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cn">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Quick-reference glossary</div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Fair value model</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">The IAS 40 alternative (fair value changes through P&amp;L) that Ind AS 40 does NOT permit for measurement.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Disclosure-only fair value</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">The fair value Ind AS 40 mandates disclosing in the notes, despite prohibiting its use for balance sheet measurement.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 14 — GLOSSARY ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <Glossary entries={[
      { term: "Fair value model", definition: "The IAS 40 alternative (fair value changes through P&L) that Ind AS 40 does NOT permit for measurement." },
      { term: "Disclosure-only fair value", definition: "The fair value Ind AS 40 mandates disclosing in the notes, despite prohibiting its use for balance sheet measurement." },
    ]} />

    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
